NAME
    ingest - import test result files or legacy logs into the store

SYNOPSIS
    ingest FILE... --runner R --tree SHA [--trial N] [--tier T]
    ingest --backfill [DIR] [--repo DIR]

DESCRIPTION
    Command of the emusen.testing module. Reads TRX files (from
    'dotnet test --logger trx') or JUnit XML files (from cargo-nextest,
    including flakyFailure and rerunFailure records) and inserts test
    rows into the testing store under their class or crate, either in a
    new trial or appended to --trial N. Files already imported (matched
    by source path) are skipped.

    With --backfill, scans DIR (default: ~/.cache/emusen/tmp) for legacy
    land/<sha>/ directories, land-<name>.log transcripts, and full-suite
    logs under wiseman-rust/, importing any runs not yet recorded. A
    land directory modified within the last hour without a .ok marker is
    treated as active and skipped. Cargo logs whose crate folder no
    longer exists at HEAD are recorded as 'cargo:?<name>'.

OPTIONS
    --runner R
        Runner identifier to attach to ingested results (required when
        importing FILE...).
    --tree SHA
        Git tree or commit SHA for the ingested run (required when
        importing FILE...).
    --trial N
        Append rows to existing trial number N instead of creating a new
        trial.
    --tier T
        Tier label recorded for the trial (default: ingest).
    --backfill [DIR]
        Scan and import historical land.sh logs under DIR.
    --repo DIR
        Git repository root for resolving crate folders during
        --backfill (overrides EMUSEN_REPO).

EXAMPLES
    ingest --backfill
    ingest results/suite-linux-x64.trx --runner ci --tree 3351e722d
    ingest target/nextest/studio/junit.xml --runner laptop --tree $(git rev-parse HEAD)

EXIT STATUS
    0   Ingestion completed.
    2   Missing required arguments, invalid flags, unreadable file, or
        store error.

SEE ALSO
    trial(1), results(1), units(1)
